FrameCryptor: stop logging raw key material (secret / salt / derived key).

Upstream webrtc-sdk/webrtc (m144_release, m150_release and every LiveKit
prebuilt built from them) prints, at RTC_LOG(LS_INFO), the input secret, the
salt and the DERIVED AES key as decimal byte lists every time a frame-cryptor
key is installed (DeriveHkdfSha256FromSecret, frame_crypto_transformer.cc:260;
DerivePBKDF2KeyFromRawKey, :284):

    secret [<32 byte values>] len 32 slat << [<salt bytes>] len 0
     derived_key [<32 byte values>] len 32

("slat" is upstream's own typo of "salt".) Any app that turns WebRTC INFO
logging on (iOS: RTCSetMinDebugLogLevel(.info); Android: logcat / Logging
severity) writes the per-call E2EE frame key into its log capture and into any
diagnostics it uploads.

This patch deletes both statements (no replacement log line, so there is
nothing to redact). The helper to_uint8_list() stays (external linkage, unused
-> no -Wunused-function). Apply AFTER aes256-framecryptor.patch and
native-pli.patch (order is not significant: the hunks do not overlap).

Verified against the byte-exact upstream blobs (git blob ecdcb30a, identical on
webrtc-sdk/webrtc@m144_release and sigarone/webrtc@f47af7bc9658-livekit-aes256-
7559.10): git apply --check passes alone and after the two existing patches.

diff --git a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
index ecdcb30..31f688a 100644
--- a/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
+++ b/api/crypto/frame_crypto_transformer.cc
@@ -257,12 +257,11 @@ int DeriveHkdfSha256FromSecret(const std::vector<uint8_t>& secret,
     return ErrorUnexpected;
   }
 
-  RTC_LOG(LS_INFO) << "secret " << to_uint8_list(secret.data(), secret.size())
-                   << " len " << secret.size() << " slat << "
-                   << to_uint8_list(salt.data(), salt.size()) << " len "
-                   << salt.size() << "\n derived_key "
-                   << to_uint8_list(derived_key.data(), derived_key.size())
-                   << " len " << derived_key.size();
+  // SECURITY: never log key material. Upstream printed the input secret, the
+  // salt and the derived key here as decimal byte lists at LS_INFO; apps that
+  // enable INFO logging (RTCSetMinDebugLogLevel(.info), logcat, ...) then leak
+  // the E2EE frame key into their log capture and any uploaded diagnostics.
+  // Removed; keep it removed when rebasing on upstream.
 
   return Success;
 }
@@ -281,13 +280,8 @@ int DerivePBKDF2KeyFromRawKey(const std::vector<uint8_t> raw_key,
     return ErrorUnexpected;
   }
 
-  RTC_LOG(LS_INFO) << "raw_key "
-                   << to_uint8_list(raw_key.data(), raw_key.size()) << " len "
-                   << raw_key.size() << " slat << "
-                   << to_uint8_list(salt.data(), salt.size()) << " len "
-                   << salt.size() << "\n derived_key "
-                   << to_uint8_list(derived_key.data(), derived_key.size())
-                   << " len " << derived_key.size();
+  // SECURITY: never log key material (raw key, salt, derived key). See the
+  // note in DeriveHkdfSha256FromSecret().
 
   return Success;
 }
